       AI Policy Toolkit 






         Scutoria AI Policy 
         Toolkit · 01 
         AI Policy Toolkit 
         01 
         Sourced. Dated. Ready to show. 
         PDF · DOCX · XLSX 




       AP-2026-MUSTER · D1 2026-10-19 · Example AI usage policy of Example Electrical Ltd In force from 19 October 2026 · version 1 This policy governs whether, under which conditions and for which purposes AI tools are used for work in this business. The business is the deployer of the tools used; the individual acts on its behalf. It applies to all employees. § 1 Permitted tools and access Use takes place through the access provided by the business. § 2 Permitted and prohibited uses Selection, assessment and termination are not based on an AI result. § 3 Prohibited inputs In case of doubt nothing is entered. Place, date, signature of the management Source-based. No legal advice. AP-2026-MUSTER AP-2026-MUSTER · D2 2026-10-19 · Example The one page to post In doubt: enter nothing, ask. The rule of doubt, what never goes into a tool, what is checked before use, where incidents are reported. Taken from the policy, so the two cannot contradict each other. Source-based. No legal advice. AP-2026-MUSTER AP-2026-MUSTER · D3 2026-10-19 · Example Tool register and approval form One row per tool actually in use, prefilled from your answers; seven questions per tool, checked at the provider; "unclear" is a finding, not a failure. Source-based. No legal advice. AP-2026-MUSTER AP-2026-MUSTER · D7 2026-10-19 · Example Evidence summary AI usage policy, nine sections in place The one page to post in place Tool register, four tools in place Briefing record partly One page, dated, with a document number: what is regulated, what is planned, what is open. Open items are listed, not hidden. Source-based. No legal advice. AP-2026-MUSTER Fact Interpretation Uncertain Gap 


         D1 D2 D3 D7 














