     Tools 
     For staff who use AI tools at work. Both run in your browser, send nothing anywhere and set no cookie. Share the link with colleagues. 





         Runs in your browser. Sends nothing. 
         May this go in? 
         Before you paste something into an AI tool: four quick questions, one traffic light, the reasons and what to do instead. 

         Example 
         What is in the text or file? None of these Which account would you use? A business account for a tool approved in the register Does the provider train its models on your inputs? I do not know What is the task? A draft, summary, translation, wording or research 
         Not yet. Clarify first. 

         Open the tool 


         Runs in your browser. Sends nothing. 
         Is there anything personal in it? 
         Paste a text. The tool marks email addresses, phone numbers, IBANs, names, addresses, health terms and access data, and replaces them with placeholders if you want. 

         Example 
         Call  [NAME]  about the offer,  [EMAIL] , site visit on  [DATE] . Invoice  [REFERENCE NO]  for  [NAME] ,  [ADDRESS] . 
         6 marked 

         Open the tool 



   Four memo generators A few questions, then a dated memo for your business: what applies, since when, what to do next, every statement with its source. You read it here; the PDF comes by email. 


         Memo by email 
         Does NIS2 apply to us? 
         Sector, size, special cases: whether your business is an essential or important entity, what that means, and the national deadlines for Austria and Germany. 
         Start 


         Memo by email 
         Must we label what our AI produces? 
         Chatbots, AI images, published texts: which of the duties of Article 50 of the AI Act apply to your business, since when, and what to do. 
         Start 


         Memo by email 
         Where does our sign-in stand? 
         Multi-factor authentication, passwords, shared accounts, leavers, recovery: eight questions, then the three steps that come first, with NIST, BSI, CISA and ENISA as sources. 
         Start 


         Memo by email 
         Where do we start with AI rules? 
         Seven questions about how AI is used in your business today, then a memo with your situation, the one first step and the plan in order, with the articles and dates. 
         Start 

