 7.3  Other member states 
 Gap  The toolkit did not search for authorities, guidance or co-determination rules in other member states. What applies everywhere: Article 4, Article 50 and the Commission's guidelines and questions and answers. What does not: the German and Austrian recommendations, which the handbook marks as such wherever it uses them. A business elsewhere checks its own chamber or data protection authority for a model and asks who the market surveillance authority is; the Commission publishes a list of the national authorities, which this handbook cites only for the missing entry for Austria (section 7.1) and has not verified for other member states. 
