 Controller 
 Stefan Dallinger, Kleinpoppen, 3902 Vitis, Austria,  kontakt@scutoria.com . Provider details are in the legal notice. 
 Principle 
 This website sets one cookie only: the session cookie of your customer account, only when you sign in and only for as long as you stay signed in (thirty days at most). It is technically necessary for signing in and needs no consent [section 165 (3) of the Austrian Telecommunications Act 2021, to be checked]. The website uses no third-party advertising or analytics services and loads no fonts or scripts from other servers. Which service providers receive data is listed in full in the sections below. 
 Hosting, database and server logs 
 The website is run and delivered on the Lovable platform; the contracting party is Lovable Labs Incorporated, 1 Lincoln St, Boston, MA 02111, USA [per Lovable's terms of service, version of 28 August 2026, to be checked]; the server programs run [on infrastructure of Cloudflare, Inc., to be checked]. Your data from the account, the generator, the waiting list and memo requests is held in a Lovable Cloud database [operated with Supabase, Inc., to be checked] in an Amazon Web Services data centre in Ireland (region eu-west-1). When you visit, these providers process technically necessary data (IP address, time, requested address, browser identifier) in logs to provide and secure the service. Log retention: [per Lovable, to be checked]. Legal basis: legitimate interest in secure operation (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR) and, for account and purchase, performance of the contract (Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR). Data processing agreement with Lovable: [agreement under Art. 28 GDPR; per Lovable only on the Business or Enterprise plan, to be checked]. Lovable is a company in the USA; where data reaches the USA or other countries outside the EEA, this happens on the basis of the EU standard contractual clauses [which Lovable incorporates in its data processing agreement, to be checked]. 
 Reach measurement without personal data 
 We count page views per day, page, language and referring domain. No IP address, browser identifier or cookie is stored; the figures cannot be linked to a person. 
 Waiting list and notification 
 If you join the waiting list, we store your email address, the chosen language and the time of your consent in order to notify you once when the first product is available. Legal basis: your consent (Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR), which you can withdraw at any time by email to  kontakt@scutoria.com . The address is deleted after the notification has been sent, at the latest after [90 days], unless you have subscribed to the newsletter. Sent via [Brevo, Sendinblue SAS, Paris; data processing agreement, to be checked]. 
 Memo generators 
 The four memo generators (NIS2, labelling under Article 50, sign-in security, where to start) take your answers through the address of the result page; nothing is stored for a memo that is only read. The business name you may enter appears in the memo and in that address. If you ask for the memo by email, we store your email address, the memo requested, its result, the chosen language and the time of your request in order to send the memo once as a PDF, and we count the request without any personal data. Legal basis: your consent (Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR), which you can withdraw at any time by email to  kontakt@scutoria.com . The address is deleted after [90 days], unless you have also asked for the notification about the next toolkit (see above) or subscribed to the newsletter. Sent via [Brevo, Sendinblue SAS, Paris; data processing agreement, to be checked]; [if the memo contact list is used: the address is kept in a contact list at Brevo for the same purpose and the same period]. 
 Newsletter 
 [To follow with the newsletter: double opt-in, content, unsubscribe, sending service, no open tracking.] 
 Purchase, invoice and payment 
 When you buy, we process your email address, invoicing details (name, address, company and VAT number where applicable), the product, the price and the time, in order to perform the contract, provide access and the invoice, and meet legal duties (Art. 6 (1) (b) and (c) GDPR). Payment is processed by Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd., 1 Grand Canal Street Lower, Dublin, Ireland. You enter your payment details (card, bank account) directly with Stripe; we do not receive them. Stripe processes those details as an independent controller for the payment [and as a processor for invoicing, tax calculation and the customer portal, to be checked]; Stripe's privacy policy: stripe.com/privacy. We keep invoicing data for seven years (section 132 of the Austrian Federal Fiscal Code). 
 Account and licence 
 In the customer account we store your email address, your answers in the generator, the generated documents and the licence status in order to provide the service (Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR). The answers may contain names, phone numbers and addresses that you enter for your documents, for example the responsible person and the deputy; you decide what you enter. Answers and documents are kept for the licence term [and twelve months after it, to be checked]; after that we delete them. You can have the account deleted at any time; invoicing data is retained because of the statutory duty. For signing in we set the session cookie named above; sign-in links are valid for thirty minutes (seven days from the welcome mail) and work once. 
 Email contact 
 If you write to us, we process your details to answer you. Legal basis: pre-contractual steps or legitimate interest in answering (Art. 6 (1) (b) and (f) GDPR). Deleted once settled, unless a retention duty applies. 
 Your rights 
 You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and objection, and the right to withdraw consent at any time. Contact  kontakt@scutoria.com . Complaints can be lodged with the Austrian Data Protection Authority: Barichgasse 40-42, 1030 Vienna, www.dsb.gv.at. 
